            <ArticleTitle>[The heart in malignant arterial hypertension: comparison of the results of morphological and electrocardiographic studies].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The electrocardiographic changes in patients with malignant arterial hypertension verified by the results of the pathoanatomic heart study have been analysed. The authors suggest a new classification of coronary arteries involvement in malignant hypertension. The informative value of Sokolov-Layon's criteria in malignant arterial hypertension is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
